      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T03:14:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`ap_pwrseq` hard-codes the timeout so needs a way to kick it out of S5 manually: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/main/zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_common_pwrseq_sm_handler.c#408",
      "parentUuid": "7d5bf439_5cced2a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1050,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1050,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "bd08eedad402193773cc410fa0898d16abaa0981",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92d36920_15bce663",
        "filename": "common/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1050,
      "author": {
        "id": 1520632
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T08:56:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Probably not a good idea. After my own testing, if s5_inactivity_timeout is 0 from the beginning, it will trigger S5G3 directly every time it goes to S5. Even driving into S0 is problematic.",
      "parentUuid": "eb3c70b8_9d054e28",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1050,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1050,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "bd08eedad402193773cc410fa0898d16abaa0981",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "727bff8e_fef27841",
        "filename": "common/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1050,
      "author": {
        "id": 1520632
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T09:07:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The function check s5_inactivity_timeout in S5\n```\nif (AP_PWRSEQ_DT_VALUE(s5_inactivity_timeout) \u003d\u003d 0)\n\t\t\treturn SYS_POWER_STATE_S5G3;\n```\n\nAnd the dts to set s5_inactivity_timeout to 0\n```\ns5-inactivity-timeout:\n    type: int\n    default: 0\n    description: |\n      Timeout in seconds for dropping back from S5 to G3.\n```\nIt will alway trigger S5G3 when powerstate into S5",
      "parentUuid": "92d36920_15bce663",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1050,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1050,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "bd08eedad402193773cc410fa0898d16abaa0981",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af1325cd_987e7775",
        "filename": "common/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1050,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T22:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, it should not be hard-coded that way. A way needs to be added to signal to the power sequencer that it should immediately drop to G3, so the reboot-on-shutdown path can send that signal then wait for the AP to reach G3.\n\nThe same functionality for legacy power sequencing (common/power.c) can be implemented in terms of setting `s5_inactivity_timeout`, but that ends up being two different implementations of the same function depending on which power sequencer a given firmware is built with.",
      "parentUuid": "727bff8e_fef27841",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1050,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1050,
        "endChar": 24
      },
